  "narration": {
    "title": "The Cardinals Crash the Party Out West",
    "intro": "The Dodgers still sit on top, but the loudest movement this week came from St. Louis, which jumped 13 spots in our power ranking. Tampa Bay is climbing too, riding a red-hot Junior Caminero. Here's the shape of the league at the moment.",
    "power_lead": "Los Angeles held first at 59-31 behind a 6-1 week, capped by seven shutout innings and ten strikeouts from Yoshinobu Yamamoto. The real jolt was St. Louis, up 13 spots after going 5-1 with a plus-24 run differential and two wins from Kyle Leahy; Tampa Bay rose three on the back of Caminero's five-homer week.",
    "offense_lead": "The Dodgers lead the team-OPS board at .791, a step clear of the Pirates at .760. Colorado and Washington sit close behind, proof that a thin record doesn't always mean a quiet lineup.",
    "staffs_lead": "Milwaukee owns the best rotation by starter ERA at 3.25, edging Tampa Bay (3.29) and the Dodgers (3.33). On the bullpen side it's Atlanta out front at 2.88, with the Yankees (3.15) the only other club under 3.20."
  }
